Explanation:

- In `postRender`, after drawing all of the vector executors (fills, strokes, text, etc.), we were unconditionally calling `super.postRender(...)`.  
- `CanvasTileLayerRenderer.postRender` composites the tile images (rasterized layers) on top of whatever is already on the canvas.  
- When your layer is in `renderMode: 'vector'`, you do *not* want those old/raster tile images—you only want the vector drawing you just did.  
- By guarding the call to `super.postRender` behind `if (renderMode !== 'vector')`, the extra translucent “ghost” layer disappears.
